# meetings: what is met with in the open country, a stretch here and there (the owner's OWN-27: a wilderness worth exploring, whose exploration regularly uncovers worthwhile destinations and interactions).
// A Kyr template (see src/world/kyr-template.ts), written for a few stretches of each country's open country (see
// src/world/region-meetings.ts, which chooses them). The country section is written once in a country; the base
// section for every meeting; of the rest, one option is drawn for each meeting from those of its land: a group is a
// kind of land (meadow, heath, wood, fen, fell; the heights draw the fell's, and heath the fell's as well as its own),
// and "any" is drawn from on every land. Each option is a small situation with an act or two, not a line.
//
// {m} is the meeting's id, to make its own ids with; {tract} the stretch it is in ("{{tract}}" its name); {town} the
// nearest town's name; {folk} the country's people; {he}, {his}, {him} whoever is met. An option with a ">> lead" line
// names a site beyond (REV-08: something met at the known edge draws the company on into the wild): {site} is its id,
// {seen} how it looks to a stranger, {toward} which way it lies from here; teaching {site}_named and {site}_found
// gives its name and the way to it. One with ">> danger" is written only away from the roads and the towns: a danger
// gives warning first. Add an option to add a meeting; nothing in the engine needs to change.
--- country
  // What has been done at a meeting, once (the pack gone through, the thanks given).
  Relation wildSpent(entity).
--- base
  // A journey across the stretch stops here the first time, for what is going on (see Travel.interrupted).
  Entity {m}_met: fact "Something is going on in {{tract}}.".
  Initially Assert staged({tract}, {m}_met).
--- wood burner 3
  // A charcoal-burner at a stack, who knows the wood: asked, tells of the place the burners keep away from, and the
  // way; helped with the stack before it flares, gives what a burner has to give.
  Person {m}_burner "the charcoal-burner" at {tract} {
    Role "a collier black to the elbows, minding a smoking stack in a clearing". Ancestry {folk}. Background laborer. Peaceable. Pronouns {he}. Manner stoic. Seen when hour(clock) >= 6 and hour(clock) < 20.
  }
  Thing {m}_stack "the charcoal stack" at {tract} {
    State flaring "A stack of cordwood under turf smokes in the clearing, and on one side the turf has slipped and flame shows through it.".
    State damped "The charcoal stack smokes evenly under its turf, as it should.".
    Change damp "Help pack fresh turf over the flaring side of the stack" from flaring to damped.
  }
  Topic {m}_burner_ask with {m}_burner "Ask the charcoal-burner about the wood" when not knows(actor, {site}_found) once {
    Says "'There's {seen} off to the {toward},' says the charcoal-burner, wiping a black hand across a black face. 'Burners don't cut near it. Things go in and don't come out, or come out wrong.' And you are told the way, as a burner tells it, by the trees.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, {site}_named). Assert knows(actor, {site}_found). }
  }
  Topic {m}_burner_thanks with {m}_burner "Tell the charcoal-burner the stack is damped down" when state({m}_stack, damped) and not wildSpent({m}_stack) once {
    Says "'You saved me a day's burn,' says the charcoal-burner, and hands over two pine-knots, pitched black and ready. 'They'll burn an hour each, in any wind. More use to you than to me.'".
    On discuss { Give 2 torch to actor. Assert wildSpent({m}_stack). }
  }
>> lead
--- wood boar 2
  // A boar where it roots: its sign first, then its warning, so that there is a moment to go round; past it, the
  // pack of someone who did not heed it.
  Observe {m}_rooting at {tract} as sign when able({m}_boar) "The ground under the oaks is rooted up in raw swathes, the earth in them still dark and wet. Whatever did it is not far off.".
  Person {m}_boar "a boar" at {tract} {
    Role "an old boar with one tusk broken, rooting for mast". Species boar. Numbers 1. Level 1. Temperament territorial. Lair {tract}.
    Warns "A boar comes out of the holly with its head low, and stands, and blows. It does not mean to go round you.".
  }
  Initially Set encounterXp({m}_boar) to 20.
  Observe {m}_pack_seen at {tract} when not wildSpent({m}_pack) "Trampled into the bracken by the rooting lies a pack, its strap broken, as if dropped by someone running.".
  Entity {m}_pack: fact "A pack trampled into the bracken.".
  Action {m}_pack_open(actor: group, site: place) "Go through the pack trampled into the bracken" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, {tract}) and not able({m}_boar) and not wildSpent({m}_pack).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert wildSpent({m}_pack). Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 7. Give herbs to actor. }
    Result "In the pack: a heel of bread gone green, a twist of dried herbs, and a purse with seven coin in it. Whoever it was did not come back for it.".
  }
>> danger
--- wood woundwort 2
  // Something to gather: a stand of woundwort, the herb the hedge-doctors bind on a cut (see data/rules/growing.kyr).
  Thing {m}_stand "the woundwort" at {tract} is scenery {
    State growing "Woundwort grows thick in a wet hollow under the trees, purple-flowered and rank-smelling: the herb the hedge-doctors bind on cuts.".
  }
  Initially Assert grows({m}_stand).
  Discovery {m}_stand_hid "What grows here is gathered, not found.".
  Item {m}_stand_1 "a bunch of woundwort" is herbs in {m}_stand hidden until {m}_stand_hid.
  Item {m}_stand_2 "a bunch of woundwort" is herbs in {m}_stand hidden until {m}_stand_hid.
  Initially Assert crop({m}_stand_1, {m}_stand). Initially Assert crop({m}_stand_2, {m}_stand).
--- wood honey 3
  // Demonstration content (Mission 19, journey 5, 7 November: an author's meeting, added as an option of this
  // template and nothing else). A honey-hunter at a wild bees' oak, one-handed on a ladder with the smoke-pot swung
  // out of reach: steadied, the comb is cut, and the thanks are what grows at the foot of the oak, the betony of
  // the catalog (data/catalog/plants.json), for stings; asked, the honey-hunter tells of the place beyond.
  Person {m}_hunter "the honey-hunter" at {tract} {
    Role "a honey-hunter up a ladder of lashed poles at a hollow oak, a veil of sacking over the face". Ancestry {folk}. Background laborer. Peaceable. Pronouns {he}. Manner cheerful. Seen when hour(clock) >= 6 and hour(clock) < 20.
  }
  Thing {m}_oak "the bees' oak" at {tract} {
    State humming "A ladder of lashed poles leans on a hollow oak, and the honey-hunter at the top of it is cutting comb out of the hollow one-handed, while the smoke-pot on its string swings out of reach and the bees rise.".
    State cut "The bees' oak hums quietly again, the hollow stopped with turf, a slab of comb gone out of it.".
    Change steady "Hold the ladder, and swing the smoke-pot up under the hollow while the comb is cut" from humming to cut.
  }
  Thing {m}_stand "the betony" at {tract} is scenery {
    State growing "Betony grows thick at the foot of the bees' oak, purple-spiked: the honey-hunter's cure for stings.".
  }
  Initially Assert grows({m}_stand).
  Discovery {m}_stand_hid "What grows here is gathered, not found.".
  Item {m}_stand_1 "a twist of betony" is betony in {m}_stand hidden until {m}_stand_hid.
  Item {m}_stand_2 "a twist of betony" is betony in {m}_stand hidden until {m}_stand_hid.
  Initially Assert crop({m}_stand_1, {m}_stand). Initially Assert crop({m}_stand_2, {m}_stand).
  Topic {m}_hunter_ask with {m}_hunter "Ask the honey-hunter about the wood" when not knows(actor, {site}_found) once {
    Says "'Bees go where they like, so I go where they go,' says the honey-hunter, pushing the sacking up. 'Except {toward}, where there's {seen}. They don't go near it, and nor do I.' And you are told the way, tree by tree.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, {site}_named). Assert knows(actor, {site}_found). }
  }
  Topic {m}_hunter_thanks with {m}_hunter "Tell the honey-hunter the comb is down safe" when state({m}_oak, cut) and not wildSpent({m}_oak) once {
    Says "'Not stung once, and that's a first,' says the honey-hunter, and breaks you off a corner of the comb to eat there and then, and pulls two twists of betony from the foot of the oak. 'For the next time. Chew it and lay it on; it takes the sting out, and stops a cut as well.'".
    On discuss { Give 2 betony to actor. Assert wildSpent({m}_oak). }
  }
>> lead
--- fell shepherd 3
  // A shepherd out after strays, who knows every fold and stone of the fell: asked, tells of the place the flock is
  // kept from, and the way; a ewe cragfast on a ledge is a thing a company could help with.
  Person {m}_herd "the shepherd" at {tract} {
    Role "a herdsman with a crook and a grey dog, out after strays". Ancestry {folk}. Background herdsman. Peaceable. Pronouns {he}. Manner grim. Seen when hour(clock) >= 6 and hour(clock) < 20.
  }
  Thing {m}_ewe "the cragfast ewe" at {tract} {
    State stuck "Below the edge a ewe stands on a ledge she jumped down to and cannot jump up from, bleating, and the shepherd's dog lying flat at the top watching her. Someone with a rope, or who can climb, could fetch her up.".
    State fetched "The ewe that was cragfast is back with the flock, as if she had never been anywhere.".
    Change fetch "Get down to the ledge and bring the cragfast ewe up" from stuck to fetched needing rope or climbing.
  }
  Topic {m}_herd_ask with {m}_herd "Ask the shepherd about the fell" when not knows(actor, {site}_found) once {
    Says "'You'll want to keep off to the {toward},' says the shepherd. 'There's {seen} over that way. My father's dogs wouldn't go near it, nor mine won't.' And you are told the way, as a shepherd knows it.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, {site}_named). Assert knows(actor, {site}_found). }
  }
  Topic {m}_herd_thanks with {m}_herd "Tell the shepherd the cragfast ewe is back with the flock" when state({m}_ewe, fetched) and not wildSpent({m}_ewe) once {
    Says "'More than I'd have got for her dead,' says the shepherd, and counts out five coin, and a heel of hard cheese wrapped in a dock leaf besides. 'There. And if you're ever up at the fold, there's a fire.'".
    On discuss { Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 5. Assert wildSpent({m}_ewe). }
  }
>> lead
--- fell wolf 2
  // A wolf over a kill: the kill seen first, then the wolf, which warns before it fights for it.
  Observe {m}_kill at {tract} as sign when able({m}_wolf) "A ewe lies torn open among the stones, not long dead, and the tracks round her are a dog's, but bigger than any dog's.".
  Person {m}_wolf "a grey wolf" at {tract} {
    Role "a lean grey wolf, alone and hungry, over its kill". Species wolf. Numbers 1. Level 1. Temperament territorial. Lair {tract}.
    Warns "A grey wolf gets up from behind the stones with blood to the eyes, and does not run. Its lip goes back from its teeth.".
  }
  Initially Set encounterXp({m}_wolf) to 20.
  Observe {m}_mark at {tract} when not able({m}_wolf) and not wildSpent({m}_mark) "The dead ewe has a shepherd's mark on her fleece, red ruddle on the shoulder: the shepherd on the fell will want to know.".
  Entity {m}_mark: fact "A wolf killed a marked ewe on the fell.".
  Action {m}_fleece(actor: group, site: place) "Cut the ruddled fleece off the dead ewe, to show whose she was" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, {tract}) and not able({m}_wolf) and not wildSpent({m}_mark).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert wildSpent({m}_mark). Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 4. }
    Result "You cut the marked fleece away. Rolled in it, where it had been tied to her neck against the wolf, are four coin: some shepherd's charm that did not work.".
  }
>> danger
--- heath yarrow 2
  // Something to gather on the heath: yarrow among the ling, which a poultice is made of.
  Thing {m}_stand "the yarrow" at {tract} is scenery {
    State growing "Among the ling a patch of yarrow grows, white flat heads and feathery leaves: the soldier's herb, for a wound.".
  }
  Initially Assert grows({m}_stand).
  Discovery {m}_stand_hid "What grows here is gathered, not found.".
  Item {m}_stand_1 "a handful of yarrow" is herbs in {m}_stand hidden until {m}_stand_hid.
  Item {m}_stand_2 "a handful of yarrow" is herbs in {m}_stand hidden until {m}_stand_hid.
  Initially Assert crop({m}_stand_1, {m}_stand). Initially Assert crop({m}_stand_2, {m}_stand).
--- fen eeler 3
  // An eel-catcher at the traps, who knows which tussocks bear a foot and which do not: asked, tells of the place
  // nobody poles to, and the way; a trap jammed in the deep channel is something to lend a hand with.
  Person {m}_eeler "the eel-catcher" at {tract} {
    Role "a fisher in a flat boat among wicker traps, with a pole twice their height". Ancestry {folk}. Background laborer. Peaceable. Pronouns {he}. Manner acerbic. Seen when hour(clock) >= 6 and hour(clock) < 20.
  }
  Thing {m}_trap "the jammed eel-trap" at {tract} {
    State jammed "One of the wicker traps is fast under a sunk branch in the deep channel, and the eel-catcher has been heaving at it a long while.".
    State freed "The wicker trap is up out of the channel, alive with eels.".
    Change free "Wade in and heave the eel-trap out from under the branch" from jammed to freed.
  }
  Topic {m}_eeler_ask with {m}_eeler "Ask the eel-catcher about the fen" when not knows(actor, {site}_found) once {
    Says "'Off to the {toward}?' says the eel-catcher. 'There's {seen}. Nobody poles that way that has any sense. But since you ask.' And you are told the way, and which ground bears a foot on the way, and which does not.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, {site}_named). Assert knows(actor, {site}_found). }
  }
  Topic {m}_eeler_thanks with {m}_eeler "Tell the eel-catcher the trap is up out of the channel" when state({m}_trap, freed) and not wildSpent({m}_trap) once {
    Says "'A week's eels in one trap,' says the eel-catcher, and gives you three coin and a pot of the black salve the fen-folk put on leech-bites. 'For your trouble. Don't wade in up to your neck, next time.'".
    On discuss { Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 3. Give bandages to actor. Assert wildSpent({m}_trap). }
  }
>> lead
--- fen lights 2
  // A light over the water where none should be: a will-o'-the-wisp, out from dusk to dawn, seen first as a light,
  // that warns as it comes (REV-03: what is met in the wild by the hour). Those who work the wild are there by day.
  Observe {m}_glim at {tract} as sign when able({m}_wisp) and (hour(clock) >= 18 or hour(clock) < 6) "Out over the black water a light goes along low, the colour of a candle, where nobody could be walking.".
  Person {m}_wisp "a will-o'-the-wisp" at {tract} {
    Role "a pale light over the fen that leads travellers into the deep water". Species wisp. Numbers 1. Level 1. Temperament territorial. Lair {tract}.
    Seen when hour(clock) >= 18 or hour(clock) < 6.
    Warns "The light comes nearer over the water, and is not a candle, and there is no one holding it. The reeds hiss.".
  }
  Initially Set encounterXp({m}_wisp) to 20.
  Observe {m}_drowned at {tract} when not able({m}_wisp) and not wildSpent({m}_drowned) "Where the light went to and fro, a pack floats snagged in the reeds: someone it led in, a long while ago.".
  Entity {m}_drowned: fact "A pack snagged in the reeds where the light was.".
  Action {m}_drowned_open(actor: group, site: place) "Pull the snagged pack out of the reeds" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, {tract}) and not able({m}_wisp) and not wildSpent({m}_drowned).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert wildSpent({m}_drowned). Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 9. Give lamp_oil to actor. }
    Result "The pack is rotten, but the purse in it is not: nine coin, and a stoppered flask of oil, dry inside.".
  }
>> danger
--- meadow haymaker 3
  // A hayward walking the bounds, who knows the country as far as the beasts are pastured: asked, tells of the place
  // the cattle are kept from, and the way; a beast through the hedge is something to help with.
  Person {m}_hayward "the hayward" at {tract} {
    Role "a bounds-keeper walking the common, with a hazel switch". Ancestry {folk}. Background farmer. Peaceable. Pronouns {he}. Manner cheerful. Seen when hour(clock) >= 6 and hour(clock) < 20.
  }
  Thing {m}_heifer "the strayed heifer" at {tract} {
    State strayed "A red heifer has broken through the hedge and stands in the next field eating what is not hers, and will not be driven by one.".
    State penned "The red heifer is back in her own field, and the gap in the hedge stopped with a hurdle.".
    Change pen "Help drive the heifer back through the gap, and stop it with a hurdle" from strayed to penned.
  }
  Topic {m}_hayward_ask with {m}_hayward "Ask the hayward about the country round about" when not knows(actor, {site}_found) once {
    Says "'Beasts won't graze to the {toward},' says the hayward. 'There's {seen} that way, past the last field. Folk from {town} don't go, but there's a way, if you want it.' And you are told it, gate by gate as far as the gates go.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, {site}_named). Assert knows(actor, {site}_found). }
  }
  Topic {m}_hayward_thanks with {m}_hayward "Tell the hayward the heifer is back in her field" when state({m}_heifer, penned) and not wildSpent({m}_heifer) once {
    Says "'There's that,' says the hayward, and gives you the fine that the heifer's owner will pay at the next court, four coin, out of a purse at the belt. 'I'll have it back off him. Go on.'".
    On discuss { Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 4. Assert wildSpent({m}_heifer). }
  }
>> lead
--- meadow meadowsweet 2
  // Something to gather in a wet field: meadowsweet, which takes a fever down.
  Thing {m}_stand "the meadowsweet" at {tract} is scenery {
    State growing "Along a wet ditch meadowsweet stands in a creamy froth, and the smell of it is like honey and almonds.".
  }
  Initially Assert grows({m}_stand).
  Discovery {m}_stand_hid "What grows here is gathered, not found.".
  Item {m}_stand_1 "a sheaf of meadowsweet" is herbs in {m}_stand hidden until {m}_stand_hid.
  Item {m}_stand_2 "a sheaf of meadowsweet" is herbs in {m}_stand hidden until {m}_stand_hid.
  Initially Assert crop({m}_stand_1, {m}_stand). Initially Assert crop({m}_stand_2, {m}_stand).
--- any cache 1
  // A store someone left against need: a sign first (stones set where no stones lie), then found by searching, and
  // taken (REV-02: where something is to be found, a sign beforehand; where nothing is, the search says so).
  Observe {m}_cairn at {tract} as sign when not knows(party, {m}_cache) "Three stones are set one on another here, where no other stones lie, and the ground at their foot has been dug and trodden flat again: somebody's mark.".
  Discovery {m}_cache "Under the three marked stones, a hollow lined with bark, and a bundle done up in oilcloth: somebody's store against need." {
    Found by searching {tract} "Under the three marked stones, a hollow lined with bark, and in it a bundle done up in oilcloth.".
  }
  Item {m}_cache_1 "a pitched torch" is torch at {tract} hidden until {m}_cache.
  Item {m}_cache_2 "a flask of lamp oil" is lamp_oil at {tract} hidden until {m}_cache.
  Item {m}_cache_3 "a roll of clean linen" is bandages at {tract} hidden until {m}_cache.
--- any waystone 2
  // A fallen stone of the old makers' road, its face under moss: cleared, a hand cut in it points the way the road
  // went, to a site beyond; one who knows the old script reads the place's name, and the way (REV-08).
  Thing {m}_stone "the fallen way-stone" at {tract} {
    State mossed "A long stone lies half sunk in the ground, squared once by a mason's tools; moss covers the face of it.".
    State cleared "The fallen way-stone lies with its face cleared: letters in the old script, and a hand cut pointing {toward}.".
    Change clear "Scrape the moss off the face of the fallen stone" from mossed to cleared.
  }
  Entity {m}_pointed: fact "A fallen way-stone of the old road points {toward}, toward {seen}.".
  Initially Assert leadsTo({m}_pointed, {site}).
  Observe {m}_hand at {tract} as sign when state({m}_stone, cleared) and not knows(party, {m}_pointed) "The hand cut in the stone points {toward}, the way the old road went: toward {seen}." teaches {m}_pointed.
  Action {m}_letters(actor: group, site: place) "Read the old letters on the way-stone" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, {tract}) and state({m}_stone, cleared) and not knows(actor, {site}_found).
    Time 1.
    Resolve check(actor, lore, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, {site}_named). Assert knows(actor, {site}_found). }
    Result "The letters are worn, but they will read: the name of the place the road went to, and how many miles, and the turns of the way.".
    Otherwise "The letters are worn past your reading. The hand still points.".
  }
>> lead
--- any tracks 2
  // Tracks of something heavy going one way: seen, they say which way the lair is; followed with a woodsman's eye,
  // they give the way to it (REV-08).
  Entity {m}_trail: fact "Heavy tracks cross the open country, going {toward}, toward {seen}.".
  Initially Assert leadsTo({m}_trail, {site}).
  Observe {m}_slots at {tract} as sign when not knows(party, {m}_trail) "Tracks cross the ground here, heavy and fresh and all going the one way, {toward}, and the same tracks older under them: something uses this way often." teaches {m}_trail.
  Action {m}_follow(actor: group, site: place) "Follow the tracks a way, and see where they go" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, {tract}) and knows(actor, {m}_trail) and not knows(actor, {site}_found).
    Time 3.
    Resolve check(actor, woodcraft, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, {site}_found). }
    Result "You follow them far enough to be sure of them: they go to {seen}, and back, by the same way every time.".
    Otherwise "You lose them on stony ground, and cast about, and do not find them again. They went {toward}; that much is certain.".
  }
>> lead
